            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-33216",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "nats-server: github.com/nats-io/nats-server: NATS-Server: Information disclosure of MQTT passwords through monitoring endpoints"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "NATS-Server is a High-Performance server for NATS.io, a cloud and edge native messaging system. Prior to versions 2.11.15 and 2.12.6, for MQTT deployments using usercodes/passwords: MQTT passwords are incorrectly classified as a non-authenticating identity statement (JWT) and exposed via monitoring endpoints. Versions 2.11.14 and 2.12.6 contain a fix. As a workaround, ensure monitoring end-points are adequately secured. Best practice remains to not expose the monitoring endpoint to the Internet or other untrusted network users."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33216",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-33216\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/nats-io/nats-server/v2\nFixed Version: 2.11.15, 2.12.6\nLink: [CVE-2026-33216](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33216)\nNATS-Server is a High-Performance server for NATS.io, a cloud and edge native messaging system. Prior to versions 2.11.15 and 2.12.6, for MQTT deployments using usercodes/passwords: MQTT passwords are incorrectly classified as a non-authenticating identity statement (JWT) and exposed via monitoring endpoints. Versions 2.11.14 and 2.12.6 contain a fix. As a workaround, ensure monitoring end-points are adequately secured. Best practice remains to not expose the monitoring endpoint to the Internet or other untrusted network users.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-33216**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/nats-io/nats-server/v2|2.11.15, 2.12.6|[CVE-2026-33216](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-33216)|\n\nNATS-Server is a High-Performance server for NATS.io, a cloud and edge native messaging system. Prior to versions 2.11.15 and 2.12.6, for MQTT deployments using usercodes/passwords: MQTT passwords are incorrectly classified as a non-authenticating identity statement (JWT) and exposed via monitoring endpoints. Versions 2.11.14 and 2.12.6 contain a fix. As a workaround, ensure monitoring end-points are adequately secured. Best practice remains to not expose the monitoring endpoint to the Internet or other untrusted network users."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 8.6,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N",
